---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import "../styles/home.css";

const description = "Independent software consultant helping teams build Elixir and Phoenix applications, improve builds and tests, and work with coding agents.";
---
<Base title="Almir Sarajčić | Software consultant" description={description} bodyClass="by-problem">
  <SiteHeader home />
  <main class="compact-wrap" id="main">
    <div class="intro">
      <p>I’m an independent software consultant. I work on Elixir and Phoenix applications and help teams improve how they build, test and ship software.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="primary" id="consulting">
      <h2>What are you working on?</h2>
      <div class="problems">
        <details>
          <summary>Need a Phoenix feature built or a bug fixed?</summary>
          <p>Add a feature, connect an API, or track down a bug in an existing Elixir or Phoenix app. For example, a LiveView workflow or a third-party integration.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Waiting too long for tests, CI or previews?</summary>
          <p>Find what slows down your builds, tests, CI or previews, and shorten the wait while keeping useful checks. For example, a slow CI job or a preview environment the team rarely uses.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Trying to use coding agents on a real codebase?</summary>
          <p>Give agents enough context and clear tasks. Put checks and independent review in the workflow. For example, a repeatable way to hand an agent a change and check what it did.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <p class="contact">Tell me a bit about your project at <a href="mailto:consulting@optimum.ba">consulting@optimum.ba</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="notes">
      <section id="building">
        <h2>What I’m building</h2>
        <p>I’m building <a href="https://kogen.dev/">Kogen</a>. You decide how a feature should work. Kogen implements it, runs the checks, gets an independent review and commits the result.</p>
        <p>I’m also putting together <a href="https://vibecodingforadults.com/">Vibe Coding for Adults</a>, a practical course for people who already use or want to start using coding agents. It covers how to write and test instructions and workflows for those agents.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="writing">
        <h2>Writing</h2>
        <ul class="writing">
          <li><a href="https://elixirdrops.net/d/9mrw2kg3">Stop mounting your LiveView twice</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://optimum.ba/blog/elixir-devops-series/">Elixir DevOps series</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://kogen.dev/notes/2026-10-30/why-i-fork-my-chatgpt-conversations/">Why I fork my ChatGPT conversations</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://kogen.dev/notes/2026-09-20/i-dont-want-agents-md/">I don’t want AGENTS.md</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://kogen.dev/notes/2026-10-26/dont-get-locked-in/">Don’t get locked in</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <footer class="compact-wrap compact-footer">
    <span>Consulting through <a href="https://optimum.ba/">Optimum Tech, LLC</a></span>
    <nav aria-label="Site information and GitHub">
      <a href="https://github.com/almirsarajcic">GitHub</a>
      <a href="/about/">About</a>
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    </nav>
  </footer>
</Base>
